/-!
# The moving seeds in the nonfixed G₂ radius branch

A nontrivial subgroup of a seed generated by its residual commutators maps
onto the entire natural six-space: the derived G₂ action is transitive on
nonzero vectors. The projection kernel centralizes the residual, so lifting
this surjectivity recovers the whole moving seed without a central error.
Applied to the derived radius, commutator idempotence and the proved seed
containment give [[V,V], Ltilde] = U in the nonfixed branch.

At an incident edge, Z = U edgeOmega follows from residual-plus-edge
generation and the defining orbit of edge centers. Thus [Z,Q_edge] lies
in U. In particular the whole critical commutator lies in both endpoint
moving seeds, and its triple commutator with the first edge lies in U_a.
All these statements concern the original ambient subgroups and maps.

These are local steps for the last paragraph of MS93 (3.8), printed p.879.
The midpoint moving-seed containment and auxiliary-subgroup contradiction
are still required to prove NonfixedCriticalEdgeInput; this module does
not assert unconditional distance-four exclusion or reconstruction.
The private import reuses the existing relative normalizer argument.
Natural coordinates retain the ATLAS attribution in LICENSES/ATLAS.txt.
-/

public noncomputable section
